
The core idea is simple: instead of making your S3 bucket publicly accessible (which is insecure), you use CloudFront as a secure reverse proxy that sits in front of your S3 bucket and serves your content

Deploy a secure static website on Amazon S3 with HTTPS, CloudFront, Origin Access Control (OAC), Route 53, and AWS Certificate Manager (ACM), following AWS security best practices.

This project demonstrates how to securely host a static website on AWS using Amazon S3 as the origin and Amazon CloudFront for content delivery. Direct public access to the S3 bucket is blocked using Origin Access Control (OAC), ensuring that all requests are served securely through CloudFront over HTTPS.

## Architecture
- Amazon S3 (Private Bucket) -Stores your website files (HTML, CSS, JS, images) securely in a private bucket
- CloudFront Distribution  - 
- Origin Access Control (OAC)
- AWS Certificate Manager (ACM)
- Route 53 (Optional Custom Domain)
- IAM Policies
- HTTPS Enforcement

## Features
- Secure private S3 bucket
- HTTPS using ACM certificate
- CloudFront CDN for global content delivery
- Origin Access Control (OAC)
- Block all public access
- Custom domain support
- Cost-effective static website hosting

## Services Used
- Amazon S3
- Amazon CloudFront
- AWS Certificate Manager (ACM)
- Amazon Route 53
- AWS IAM

## Security Best Practices
- Block Public Access enabled
- Least privilege IAM policies
- CloudFront as the only access path to S3
- HTTPS-only access
- Bucket policy restricted to CloudFront  

## The Architecture Works (Step by Step):
- User types www.example.com in their browser
- Route 53 resolves the domain to the CloudFront distribution
- CloudFront terminates SSL/TLS (HTTPS) and routes the request to the appropriate edge location
- If WAF is enabled, it checks for threats before forwarding
- CloudFront fetches the file from the private S3 bucket using OAC/OAI
- S3 serves the file (only because CloudFront is authorized)
- CloudFront caches the response for future requests.

## This Architecture Makes Sense:
- Cost-effective: Pay only for what you use (S3 storage + CloudFront data transfer)
- Scalable: Handles traffic spikes automatically (serverless)
- Fast: Global CDN delivers content from nearest edge location
- Secure: Multiple layers of protection without complex configuration
- Maintainable: Infrastructure as Code (Terraform) means repeatable, version-controlled deployments
- User receives the content securely and quickly
